01:03:14.965 --> 01:03:16.840
completely moot.

01:03:16.840 --> 01:03:17.830
- I mean there's something known

01:03:17.830 --> 01:03:19.390
as the sports illustrated curse.

01:03:19.390 --> 01:03:21.422
I don't know if people know what this is,

01:03:21.422 --> 01:03:24.050
and the idea is that if you
get a picture on the cover

01:03:24.050 --> 01:03:25.100
of sports illustrated,

01:03:25.100 --> 01:03:27.100
you're gonna go into a slump afterwards.

01:03:28.390 --> 01:03:29.830
The obvious explanation of that

01:03:29.830 --> 01:03:32.263
is that sports is (indistinct) reverting.

01:03:33.310 --> 01:03:34.510
You're gonna end up on the cover

01:03:34.510 --> 01:03:35.750
when you're at the end of a hot streak,

01:03:35.750 --> 01:03:37.947
and you're gonna mean revert.

01:03:37.947 --> 01:03:39.680
The worst thing that could
happen to you in the pandemic

01:03:39.680 --> 01:03:42.240
was to be on the cover of
scientific American as like,

01:03:42.240 --> 01:03:43.700
look how well India is doing,

01:03:43.700 --> 01:03:45.985
look how well New Mexico is doing.

01:03:45.985 --> 01:03:48.180
That was the sports illustrated curse.

01:03:48.180 --> 01:03:51.370
It was guaranteed, if somebody
wrote you off as a case study

01:03:51.370 --> 01:03:53.100
in how to manage the pandemic,

01:03:53.100 --> 01:03:55.700
that within two months tops,

01:03:55.700 --> 01:03:59.273
you were gonna be a poster
child of what not to do,

01:04:00.602 --> 01:04:03.220
we watched this happen week after week,

01:04:03.220 --> 01:04:04.620
and month after month, yeah.

01:04:06.566 --> 01:04:08.974
- So there's a very interesting question

01:04:08.974 --> 01:04:11.600
from Carl (indistinct) who asks,

01:04:11.600 --> 01:04:15.080
